{"id": "EUVD-2026-97583", "enisaUuid": "17f1a43d-3877-3a97-b195-8a0d018d3498", "description": "ImageMagick 7.1.0-21 before 7.1.2-32 contains a heap buffer over-read in its handling of the -fx option, where a certain -fx operation reads beyond the bounds of an allocated heap buffer in specific situations. Attackers who can get a crafted -fx expression processed can read out-of-bounds heap memory, potentially disclosing limited memory contents.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T16:04:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:42:56", "baseScore": 4.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/security/advisories/GHSA-cvgp-q487-j22w", "https://github.com/ImageMagick/ImageMagick/commit/0e82a4d0b294581186ed7b3e1dce59c858a73dba", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/imagemagick-7.1.0-21-before-7.1.2-32-heap-buffer-over-read-via-fx-option"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8hfc-qgqf-ghwj", "CVE-2026-109281"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d414f5b4-ab87-319f-9724-592c39262c9e", "product": {"name": "ImageMagick", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}, "product_version": "7.1.0-21 <7.1.2-32"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c7e9a225-3973-3e4f-ba69-13ab928b1776", "vendor": {"name": "ImageMagick"}}], "isExploited": false}